<section class="wrap development" id="development"><div class="section-top"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / WEB & DEVELOPMENT</span><h2>More than<br>what meets the eye.</h2></div><p>Responsive frontends and practical software projects. Explore the experience, then look under the hood.</p></div><article class="web-feature"><div class="web-art"><span class="web-tag">FRONTEND / ARABIC RTL</span><div class="browser-mock"><div class="browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>wasla / web experience</span></div><div class="mock-content"><img src="assets/wasla-mark.svg" alt="Wasla" width="46" height="46"><span lang="ar" dir="rtl">فرصتك القادمة تبدأ هنا.</span><p>A thoughtful journey.<br>A clearer next step.</p><div class="mock-cards"><div>Discover <b>↗</b></div><div>Prepare <b>✓</b></div><div>Apply <b>→</b></div></div></div></div><span class="art-note">6 PAGES · RESPONSIVE · REUSABLE COMPONENTS</span></div><div class="web-copy"><span class="category">FEATURED DEVELOPMENT PROJECT</span><h3>Wasla frontend</h3><p>A complete Arabic marketing frontend for a job-search assistant. Six responsive pages, right-to-left layouts, animated product sections and interactive FAQs.</p><p class="muted">My role: frontend development. Additional backend contributions were made outside this frontend repository.</p><div class="tags"><span>Next.js</span><span>React</span><span>TypeScript</span><span>Tailwind CSS</span></div><div class="link-row"><a class="button dark" href="https://wasla-agent-demo.mega12-kma12.chatgpt.site" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View live demo ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/elmlahym-wq/wasla-frontend" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View source ↗</a></div></div></article><div class="code-projects"><article><span class="code-icon">{ ↗ }</span><span class="category">AUTOMATION / PYTHON</span><h3>Instagram Comment-to-DM</h3><p>A campaign dashboard connecting keyword-matching comments with public and private replies through the Meta Graph API. Includes webhook validation and duplicate-event handling.</p><div class="tags"><span>Python</span><span>FastAPI</span><span>SQLAlchemy</span></div><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/elmlahym-wq/ig-automation2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore repository ↗</a></article><article><span class="code-icon">{ / }</span><span class="category">REST API / TRAINING PROJECT</span><h3>Employee REST API</h3><p>A Java service for listing and adding employees, with unit and HTTP tests. Built during the HPE Software Engineering Job Simulation on Forage.</p><div class="tags"><span>Java</span><span>Spring Boot</span><span>Maven</span><span>JUnit</span></div><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/elmlahym-wq/hpe-employee-rest-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore repository ↗</a></article></div></section>
<section class="about wrap" id="about"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</span><h2>Creative curiosity.<br>Engineering mindset.</h2><p class="about-lead">I’m Mohamed, a Computer Systems Engineering student based in Gaza, Palestine. I combine AI-assisted creative production with frontend development and programming.</p><p>I work from a clear brief, explore visual directions and refine the details—pacing, transitions, layout and consistency—until the work fits its purpose.</p><a class="text-link" href="assets/Mohamed_Elmalahi_CV.pdf?v=20261018" target="_blank">View my CV ↗</a></div><div class="about-details"><div class="detail-row"><span>EDUCATION</span><div><b>Al-Azhar University — Gaza</b><p>Computer Systems Engineering · In progress<br>Second year · Average: 94.1%</p></div></div><div class="detail-row"><span>MY TOOLKIT</span><div><b>Creative production + development</b><p>Motion graphics · Animation · Visual storytelling<br>Frontend development · Python · C<br>Prompt development · Iterative refinement</p></div></div><div class="detail-row"><span>CONTINUED LEARNING</span><div><b>Training & certificates</b><p>HPE Software Engineering Simulation · Forage<br>Web Application Penetration Testing · 30 hours<br>Hands-on practice in authorized training labs</p><a href="https://academy.claude.com/verify/4d42db1b52e0bd5d75b29867526eec18" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Claude 101 ↗</a><br><a href="https://academy.claude.com/verify/d116eb5aaa82fd7d42d160527524b465" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AI Capabilities and Limitations ↗</a></div></div><div class="detail-row"><span>LANGUAGES</span><div><b>Arabic · English</b><p>Native Arabic · English B2+ (self-assessed)</p></div></div></div></section>
